  "caption": "An athlete performs a standing long jump on a track, oriented to the right. From an upright stance with arms overhead (held until ~2.58s), the athlete executes a preparatory dip by crouching deeply and swinging both arms backward simultaneously between 2.78s and 3.68s. The propulsive phase follows immediately: arms swing forward and upward while legs extend for takeoff between 3.98s and 4.48s, leaving the ground by ~4.5s. During flight (4.48s–4.88s), the body extends fully before knees draw forward for landing. Upon contact at 4.88s, the athlete absorbs impact into a deep squat until ~5.48s, then rises back to an upright position with arms overhead by 6.88s. Concurrently, Mandarin narration explains methods to improve standing long jump performance ('如何在一分钟之内就立竿见影...'), accompanied by intermittent sharp transient sounds unrelated to specific footfalls or impacts in the video timeline.",
